    <DataNode elementId="MONOMER-17354" textLabel="MONOMER-17354" type="Protein">
      <Xref identifier="MONOMER-17354" dataSource="plantcyc" />
      <Graphics centerX="450" centerY="455" width="90.0" height="25.0" textColor="000000" fontName="Arial" fontWeight="Normal" fontStyle="Normal" fontDecoration="Normal" fontStrikethru="Normal" fontSize="12" hAlign="Center" vAlign="Middle" borderColor="000000" borderStyle="Solid" borderWidth="1.0" fillColor="FFFFFF" shapeType="Rectangle" />
      <Comment source="PMN, zhang">A phosphatidate kinase (PA kinase) activity was detected from cell suspension cultures of Catharanthus roseus |CITS: [12231900]|. PA kinase activity was also detected from 16 other plant species, spanning across the entire plant kingdom. Interestingly, it was not detected in mammals. The PA kinase of Catharanthus roseus was partially purified and its properties were further characterized |CITS: [12232252]|. The kinase activity was very specific for phosphatidate. Neither lysophosphatidate nor other lipids tested was phosphorylated. Specific enzyme activities (in the range of 3-4 umol/min/mg) were comparable towards difference species of PA tested, including dipalmitoyl, distearoyl, dioleoyl, and 1-stearoyl-2-arachidonoyl PA.The enzyme accepted either ATP or GTP, with Km values of 12 and 18 uM, respectively. The enzyme activity depends on the presence of surfactants such as Triton X-100 or beta-octylglucoside.</Comment>
      <Property key="UniqueID" value="MONOMER-17354" />
      <Property key="Catalyzes" value="RXN-20356" />
      <Property key="InstanceNameTemplate" value="MONOMER-*" />
      <Property key="MolecularWeightExp" value="39." />
      <Property key="MolecularWeightKd" value="39." />
      <Property key="Pi" value="4.8" />
      <CitationRef elementRef="citation_PUB_12231900" />
      <CitationRef elementRef="citation_PUB_12232252" />
    </DataNode>
