    <DataNode elementId="MONOMER-AT1G15080" textLabel="Lipid phosphate phosphatase 2" type="Protein">
      <Xref identifier="Q9XI60" dataSource="uniprot" />
      <Graphics centerX="900" centerY="455" width="90.0" height="25.0" textColor="000000" fontName="Arial" fontWeight="Normal" fontStyle="Normal" fontDecoration="Normal" fontStrikethru="Normal" fontSize="12" hAlign="Center" vAlign="Middle" borderColor="000000" borderStyle="Solid" borderWidth="1.0" fillColor="FFFFFF" shapeType="Rectangle" />
      <Comment source="pmngroup">Two isoforms of lipid phosphate phosphatase exist in Arabidopsis. The two isoforms take both |FRAME: DIACYLGLYCEROL-PYROPHOSPHATE a 1,2-diacyl-&lt;i&gt;sn&lt;/i&gt;-glycerol 3-diphosphate| (DGPP) and |FRAME: L-PHOSPHATIDATE a 1,2-diacyl-&lt;i&gt;sn&lt;/i&gt;-glycerol-3-phosphate| as substrates. Isoform |FRAME: AT2G01180 LPP1| has a preference of DGPP for substrate, whereas isoform |FRAME: AT1G15080 LPP2| does not have preference over the two substrates |CITS: [11278556]|.</Comment>
      <Property key="UniqueID" value="MONOMER-AT1G15080" />
