    <DataNode elementId="AT4G30340-MONOMER" textLabel="diacylglycerol kinase" type="Protein">
      <Xref identifier="B0KYU1" dataSource="uniprot" />
      <Graphics centerX="300" centerY="535" width="90.0" height="25.0" textColor="000000" fontName="Arial" fontWeight="Normal" fontStyle="Normal" fontDecoration="Normal" fontStrikethru="Normal" fontSize="12" hAlign="Center" vAlign="Middle" borderColor="000000" borderStyle="Solid" borderWidth="1.0" fillColor="FFFFFF" shapeType="Rectangle" />
      <Comment source="pmngroup">The Arabidopsis genome contains 7 candidate diacylglycerol kinase (DAG kinase) genes. Two of them, AtDGK2 (At5G63770) and AtDGK7 (At4G30340) were characterized and shown for DAG kinase activities in vitro |CITS: [16081412]|. The specific activities of AtDGK2 and AtDGK7 were in the range of 0.5-3 pmol/min/ug. Both enzymes phosphorylated DAG species that are physiologically important in plants, including 1,2-dioleoyl-sn-glycerol, 1-palmitoyl-2-oleoyl-sn-glycerol, 1-oleoyl-2-palmitoyl-sn-glycerol, and 1-stearoyl-2-linoleoyl-sn-glycerol.</Comment>
      <Property key="UniqueID" value="AT4G30340-MONOMER" />
      <Property key="AlternativeId_Araport" value="AT4G30340.1" />
      <Property key="AlternativeId_Smart" value="SM00046" />
