      <Comment source="pmngroup">The Arabidopsis genome contains 7 candidate diacylglycerol kinase (DAG kinase) genes. Two of them, AtDGK2 (At5G63770) and AtDGK7 (At4G30340) were characterized and shown for DAG kinase activities in vitro |CITS: [16081412]|. The specific activities of AtDGK2 and AtDGK7 were in the range of 0.5-3 pmol/min/ug. Both enzymes phosphorylated DAG species that are physiologically important in plants, including 1,2-dioleoyl-sn-glycerol, 1-palmitoyl-2-oleoyl-sn-glycerol, 1-oleoyl-2-palmitoyl-sn-glycerol, and 1-stearoyl-2-linoleoyl-sn-glycerol.</Comment>
