    <DataNode elementId="MONOMER-17355" textLabel="MONOMER-17355" type="Protein">
      <Xref identifier="MONOMER-17355" dataSource="plantcyc" />
      <Graphics centerX="450" centerY="615" width="90.0" height="25.0" textColor="000000" fontName="Arial" fontWeight="Normal" fontStyle="Normal" fontDecoration="Normal" fontStrikethru="Normal" fontSize="12" hAlign="Center" vAlign="Middle" borderColor="000000" borderStyle="Solid" borderWidth="1.0" fillColor="FFFFFF" shapeType="Rectangle" />
      <Comment source="PMN, zhang">A diacylglycerol kinase (DAG kinase) activity was found in the plasma membrane fraction of cultured Catharanthus roseus cells |CITS: [16668739]|. The DAG kinase is an intrinsic membrane protein since no activity was found in the cytosol. DAG kinase activity was dependent on phospholipids, including negatively charged ones such as phosphatidylinositol and phosphatidylglycerol, as well as bisphosphatidylglycerol. Enzyme activity was also dependent on the presence of deoxycholate and Triton X-100. Maximum activity was achieved with an addition of a combination of phospholipid, deoxycholate and Triton X-100. The DAG kinase used both ATP and GTP equally well.</Comment>
      <Property key="UniqueID" value="MONOMER-17355" />
      <Property key="Catalyzes" value="RXN-20357" />
      <Property key="InstanceNameTemplate" value="MONOMER-*" />
      <CitationRef elementRef="citation_PUB_16668739" />
    </DataNode>
